* Rohm BA662 (IC15, docs/circuit.md section 6.1): OTA and output buffer, SIP-9.
*   1 C (I_ABC in)  2 -IN  3 +IN  4 buffer bias  5 -V  6 OTA out  7 buffer in  8 buffer out  9 +V
*
* No Rohm data sheet or SPICE model of the BA662 exists. BA662 is built from:
* - Open Music Labs' internal circuit, reverse engineered from an original BA662 by driving its
*   pins (http://wiki.openmusiclabs.com/wiki/BA662, .../x0xb0x): a two-transistor control-current
*   mirror (as the CA3080), a differential pair into three-transistor Wilson mirrors (as the
*   LM13700), and an NPN/PNP complementary follower whose bias current is set from pin 4 (as the
*   BA6110). Measured on the original: emitter resistors of ~500 ohm on the control mirror, a 1:1
*   buffer bias mirror, and the buffer's pull-up (10k).
* - Alfa's AS662 (a BA662 clone) data sheet, 2021 v1: the same circuit, with control-mirror
*   emitter resistors 400 ohm, buffer bias resistor 40k, buffer collector resistor 500 ohm and
*   pull-up 10k (+-20 %).
* - Rohm's BA6110 data sheet (same maker, same buffer): pull-up 11k, gm 4800-12000 uS (typ 8000)
*   at I_ABC 500 uA, OTA output to within ~1 V of the rails.
* The transistors are generic IC devices of the period (vertical NPN, lateral PNP for the
* Wilson mirrors, substrate PNP in the buffer); the circuit's gain depends on matching, not on
* their parameters. Spread: .param ba_bfn (NPN gain), ba_bfp (lateral PNP gain), ba_is (NPN saturation
* current: the I_ABC input's diode drop), ba_re (control
* mirror emitter resistors), ba_rpu (buffer pull-up).
.param ba_bfn=200 ba_bfp=50 ba_re=450 ba_rpu=10k ba_is=5e-16
.model BA662N NPN(IS={ba_is} BF={ba_bfn} VAF=100 BR=1 RB=200 RE=2 RC=50 IKF=10m
+ CJE=0.6p CJC=0.5p CJS=1.5p TF=0.4n)
.model BA662LP PNP(IS=5e-16 BF={ba_bfp} VAF=50 BR=1 RB=150 RE=5 RC=100 IKF=0.5m
+ CJE=0.4p CJC=1p TF=25n)
.model BA662SP PNP(IS=5e-16 BF={1.5*ba_bfp} VAF=60 BR=1 RB=150 RE=5 RC=50 IKF=3m
+ CJE=0.6p CJC=1.5p TF=3n)

.subckt BA662 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9
* control-current mirror: pin 1 into the diode side, the other side is the pair's tail
Q1B 1 1 e1b BA662N
R1B e1b 5 {ba_re}
Q1A tail 1 e1a BA662N
R1A e1a 5 {ba_re}
* differential pair
Q2A ca 2 tail BA662N
Q2B cb 3 tail BA662N
* -IN side: PNP Wilson mirror (Q3B diode, Q3A, Q5A), its output into the NPN Wilson mirror
Q3B x1 x1 9 BA662LP
Q3A ca x1 9 BA662LP
Q5A o1 ca x1 BA662LP
Q6B y y 5 BA662N
Q6A o1 y 5 BA662N
Q7B 6 o1 y BA662N
* +IN side: PNP Wilson mirror sourcing into pin 6
Q4B x2 x2 9 BA662LP
Q4A cb x2 9 BA662LP
Q5B 6 cb x2 BA662LP
* buffer: Q7A NPN follower on a current sink set from pin 4, Q8A PNP follower with pull-up
R3 4 nb 40k
Q9B nb nb 5 BA662N
Q9A e7 nb 5 BA662N
R4 9 c7 500
Q7A c7 7 e7 BA662N
Q8A 5 e7 8 BA662SP
R5 9 8 {ba_rpu}
.ends BA662

* The textbook OTA the voice model uses (core/voice.cpp vcaStep): output current
* I_ABC tanh(v/2V_T) with I_ABC the current into pin 1 (which sits at a diode drop), unlimited
* output swing and an ideal unity buffer. Pins 4 and 9 are unused.
.subckt BA662IDEAL 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9
D1 1 n1 BA662ID
Vabc n1 5 0
Bota 5 6 I = I(Vabc)*tanh((V(3)-V(2))/(2*0.025865))
Ebuf 8 5 7 5 1
.model BA662ID D(IS=2e-15)
.ends BA662IDEAL
